**Reused evidence**
- None accepted from the prior thread for Chapter 1B.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Presiden Joko Widodo dan Wakil Presiden Ma'ruf Amin Dilantik di MPR","publisher":"Presiden RI","publication_date":"2019-10-20","url":"https://presidenri.go.id/siaran-pers/presiden-joko-widodo-dan-wakil-presiden-maruf-amin-dilantik-di-mpr/","claim":"Joko Widodo and Ma'ruf Amin were formally inaugurated for the 2019-2024 presidential term.","locator":"headline and opening paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidency site with a dated inauguration notice and direct officeholder identification.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Establishes Jokowi's office during the 2022 period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct attribution to Jokowi as officeholder; this is office status, not policy performance.","contrary_evidence":[],"lenses":["1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indonesia 1945 (reinst. 1959, rev. 2002) Constitution","publisher":"Constitute Project","publication_date":"current consolidated text","url":"https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/Indonesia_2002","claim":"The President holds executive power, may submit bills, issue implementing regulations, and is assisted by a Vice-President and ministers whom the President appoints and dismisses.","locator":"Article 4, Article 5, Article 17","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Constitutional text directly states executive authority and cabinet appointment/removal powers.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Defines Jokowi's actual 2022 executive authority.","ruler_attribution":"Direct institutional authority; these powers belong to the Indonesian presidency, not to Jokowi personally alone.","contrary_evidence":["Legislative bargaining and coalition politics can constrain how much of this authority is usable in practice."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indonesia 1945 (reinst. 1959, rev. 2002) Constitution","publisher":"Constitute Project","publication_date":"current consolidated text","url":"https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/Indonesia_2002","claim":"The President serves a five-year term with only one reelection, is supreme commander of the armed forces, and may declare war, make peace, and conclude treaties with DPR approval.","locator":"Article 7, Article 10, Article 11","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Constitutional text directly fixes the term ceiling and the treaty/war powers relevant to existential-risk exposure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Defines the 2022 ceiling and the absence of open-ended tenure or nuclear command authority.","ruler_attribution":"Direct institutional authority; Jokowi had war/treaty powers only within constitutional approval rules.","contrary_evidence":["Indonesia is not a nuclear-armed state, so these powers do not translate into nuclear-use authority."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.4","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"United Nations Treaty Collection","publication_date":"1980-07-14","url":"https://treaties.un.org/Pages/showActionDetails.aspx?clang=_en&objid=08000002801207b4","claim":"Indonesia ratified the NPT.","locator":"Action details page, ratification entry for Indonesia","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN Treaty Collection ratification record is authoritative for treaty status and dates.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Structural baseline for Indonesia's nonproliferation posture in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State-level commitment, inherited by Jokowi; not a 2022 personal decision.","contrary_evidence":["Treaty ratification predates Jokowi and does not by itself show 2022 conduct."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indonesia Deposits Instrument of Ratification to the Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty","publisher":"UNODA","publication_date":"2012-02-06","url":"https://archive-disarmament.unoda.org/news/indonesia-ctbt/","claim":"Indonesia deposited its CTBT ratification instrument at the UN in 2012 and became the 157th state to ratify the treaty.","locator":"paragraphs 1-2","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN disarmament office notice gives the date, act, and treaty significance directly.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Baseline treaty posture in force during 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State-level treaty commitment predating Jokowi; relevant as inherited posture.","contrary_evidence":["CTBT is not in force globally, so ratification is normative but not a complete arms-control endpoint."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treaty on the Southeast Asia Nuclear-Weapon-Free Zone (Bangkok Treaty)","publisher":"United Nations Platform for Nuclear-Weapon-Free Zones","publication_date":"current page","url":"https://www.un.org/nwfz/content/treaty-bangkok","claim":"The Bangkok Treaty obliges parties not to develop, manufacture, acquire, possess, station, transport, test, or use nuclear weapons, and to use nuclear material and facilities exclusively for peaceful purposes.","locator":"Overview section","source_type":"official/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN nuclear-weapon-free-zone page summarizes the treaty's core obligations and membership.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly shapes Indonesia's nuclear posture in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State-level obligation; Jokowi inherited and administered within this legal framework.","contrary_evidence":["The treaty does not eliminate all regional nuclear risk because external nuclear-weapon-state assurances remained incomplete."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.5","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNODA 2022 Yearbook, Chapter 4","publisher":"United Nations Office for Disarmament Affairs","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://yearbook-archive.unoda.org/2022/chapter4.html","claim":"In 2022 ASEAN leaders reaffirmed preserving Southeast Asia as a zone free of nuclear weapons and other weapons of mass destruction, and the Plan of Action to Strengthen the Implementation of the Bangkok Treaty was renewed for 2023-2027.","locator":"Treaty on the Southeast Asia Nuclear Weapon-Free Zone section","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"UN yearbook provides contemporaneous regional summary, though it is not a direct Jokowi statement.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Matches the 2022 regional environment in which Indonesia operated.","ruler_attribution":"Regional/ASEAN posture rather than personal Jokowi conduct; still relevant to the inherited baseline.","contrary_evidence":["The same source notes that none of the five nuclear-weapon states had signed the Bangkok Treaty protocol by end-2022."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.6","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Country List : Office of Legal Affairs : IAEA","publisher":"International Atomic Energy Agency","publication_date":"current page","url":"https://ola.iaea.org/Applications/FactSheets/Country/Detail?code=ID","claim":"Indonesia had the NPT safeguards agreement in force since 1980 and an Additional Protocol with the IAEA signed in 1999.","locator":"Safeguards Agreements table","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IAEA country fact sheet is the authoritative status source for safeguards agreements.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Structural safeguard baseline for 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State-level nuclear safety and verification architecture inherited by Jokowi.","contrary_evidence":["Safeguards reduce diversion risk but do not by themselves prove zero misuse risk."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Preparation of Standard Operating Procedure for Physical Protection October 25, 2022","publisher":"BAPETEN","publication_date":"2022-10-25","url":"https://bapeten.go.id/berita/preparation-of-standard-operating-procedure-for-physical-protection-october-25-2022-151958?lang=en","claim":"BAPETEN said its task is to ensure nuclear utilization is only for peaceful purposes and to protect nuclear materials and installations by applicable international standards; it also noted Indonesia's CPPNM and amendment ratifications.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct regulator statement in 2022 about peaceful use, physical protection, and treaty compliance.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 institutional posture under Jokowi's administration.","ruler_attribution":"Government/regulatory posture, not proof of Jokowi's personal involvement, but within his executive authority.","contrary_evidence":["This is operational safety governance, not an existential-risk breakthrough or a nuclear-weapons decision."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PP No. 52 Tahun 2022","publisher":"BPK JDIH","publication_date":"2022-12-12","url":"https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/232967/pp-no-52-tahun-2022","claim":"PP 52/2022 regulates safety, security, and management across all stages of nuclear-mineral mining and imposes administrative sanctions for security violations.","locator":"abstrak peraturan and metadata","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official regulation abstract clearly states scope, enforcement, and enactment date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruler-period action in peaceful nuclear governance.","ruler_attribution":"Government action under Jokowi's presidency; direct personal authorship is not shown in the abstract.","contrary_evidence":["The rule is about mining and safety, not nuclear weapons or command-and-control risk."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"BAPETEN Receives Consultation Request for Nuclear Power Plant Development","publisher":"BAPETEN","publication_date":"2022-12-13","url":"https://bapeten.go.id/berita/bapeten-receives-consultation-request-for-nuclear-power-plant-development-150706?lang=id","claim":"BAPETEN received a consultation request from PT ThorCon Power Indonesia for an NPP, and the consultation framework included a roadmap for NPP design development and safety to be implemented in 2023.","locator":"lines 82-94","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct regulator notice with date, parties, and technical scope for the consultation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 energy-policy and nuclear-infrastructure context.","ruler_attribution":"Government-regulatory context under Jokowi; the source does not show a personal presidential decision, only a state process.","contrary_evidence":["It shows exploratory civilian nuclear planning, not weapons policy or catastrophic escalation."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"BRIN, ThorCon Power ink MoU on nuclear power plant prototype","publisher":"ANTARA News","publication_date":"2022-02-11","url":"https://en.antaranews.com/news/214677/brin-thorcon-power-ink-mou-on-nuclear-power-plant-prototype","claim":"BRIN and ThorCon Power Indonesia signed an MoU on R&D for molten-salt reactors as future NPP candidates and a prototype.","locator":"lines 63-67","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting on a public R&D agreement, with clear institutional attribution.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Matches early-2022 civilian nuclear exploration.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional, not direct personal Jokowi conduct; still relevant to the state's risk posture.","contrary_evidence":["A research MoU is not a construction decision, and it does not show a weapons or emergency escalation choice."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Govt mulling Russia's offer to develop nuclear energy in Indonesia","publisher":"ANTARA News","publication_date":"2022-07-04","url":"https://en.antaranews.com/news/237681/govt-mulling-russia-s-offer-to-develop-nuclear-energy-in-indonesia","claim":"The energy minister said the government was considering Russia's offer to develop an NPP, while the national roadmap projected nuclear energy need only starting around 2040.","locator":"lines 63-68","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Reporting is direct and dated, but the claim is ministerial and roadmap-based rather than a presidential act.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 policy discussion on civilian nuclear power.","ruler_attribution":"Government-level consideration under Jokowi; not a direct personal nuclear-risk choice by the president.","contrary_evidence":["The article presents nuclear as a long-range energy option, not an urgent security necessity."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Dangers Posed by Nuclear Weapons Back in Global Spotlight, United Nations High Representative for Disarmament Affairs Tells First Committee","publisher":"UN Press","publication_date":"2022-10-17","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/gadis3682.doc.htm","claim":"Indonesia, speaking on behalf of NAM, reaffirmed the need for multilateral nuclear disarmament, supported CTBT, and emphasized that nuclear-weapon-free zones strengthen nonproliferation.","locator":"Indonesia (on behalf of the Non-Aligned Movement) statement","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN meeting record captures a dated official statement from the Indonesian delegation.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Matches 2022 multilateral nuclear posture.","ruler_attribution":"Attribution is to Indonesia's delegation, not a direct Jokowi statement; still useful as state posture context.","contrary_evidence":["This is diplomatic posture, not evidence of a ruler-level command or crisis choice in 2022."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.4","1B.6","1B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Non-Nuclear-Armed States Get Nothing in Return for Fulfilling Commitments Except Threat of Potential Annihilation, First Committee Told","publisher":"UN Press","publication_date":"2022-10-20","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/gadis3690.doc.htm","claim":"Indonesia told the First Committee that nuclear-weapon states should comply with their obligations, eliminate arsenals transparently, and that nuclear safety and security norms should be pursued within the IAEA framework.","locator":"Indonesia statement in the 'Statements' section","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN meeting record preserves the statement and its policy content directly.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 nuclear diplomacy context.","ruler_attribution":"State-level foreign-policy line rather than direct presidential choice.","contrary_evidence":["Again, this is a multilateral statement, not evidence of Jokowi personally managing a nuclear crisis."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.3","1B.4","1B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I considered roughly 30 documents across treaty databases, UNODA yearbooks, IAEA/BAPETEN regulatory pages, presidency/cabinet releases, and reporting.
- Strongly relevant but rejected as out-of-period: Jokowi's 2015 "No" on near-term nuclear power plant construction, later 2023-2026 BAPETEN/IAEA follow-up pages, and post-2022 world-nuclear profile material.
- Relevant but downgraded to context because attribution is institutional rather than personal: BRIN-ThorCon MoU, Russia-offer coverage, and UN First Committee statements by Indonesian diplomats.
- Rejected as off-topic for Chapter 1B: climate-finance and coal-transition pieces, battery/industrialization articles, IKN coverage, fuel-price, corruption, and general governance stories.
- Rejected/unused duplicates: multiple treaty-status pages that repeated the same NPT/CTBT/SEANWFZ facts without adding a materially distinct claim.
- Blocked or unusable: some Kompas/Tempo/other pages were inaccessible through robots or were only useful as secondary echoes of the same facts.

**Remaining gaps**
- I did not find a 2022 source showing Jokowi personally making a uniquely nuclear-weapons, command-and-control, or brinkmanship decision. More searching would probably not change that materially.
- I found only limited civil-nuclear exposure: safety regulation, mining rules, and NPP feasibility/consultation work. If you want tighter attribution, the best next targets would be direct 2022 presidential or cabinet transcripts on PP 52/2022, the National Energy Council roadmap, or any presidential remarks on NPP feasibility.
- I did not find any 2022 evidence of nuclear rhetoric, proliferation pressure, or crisis de-escalation involving Jokowi personally. More search could refine the negative finding, but it is unlikely to uncover a material 1B risk-bearing choice.
- The strongest current read is limited exposure with peaceful-nuclear governance choices, not a nuclear-risk leadership record in the strict 1B sense.
